    pm:receptionCircumstance "By the account on pp. 16-17, Van Tassel learned to tune in to vibrations by long study of his own thought, then gathered a small group at regular scheduled meetings to add power to the reception; the message is spoken aloud through his physical body, which he likens to a loudspeaker, and taken down in shorthand, and he says it is given in words humans can understand. The publisher's note of the New Age printing, signed Franklin Thomas, adds that he receives in attunement with the frequency of the communicating intelligence, mostly while his body senses involuntarily, in a condition in which he does not know his hearers are there, sometimes with partial awareness of them. No record of the sessions other than the printed text is mentioned. Dated 6 July 1952. The author reports that about 23 members present felt alike a sensation of warm fluid running over their bodies." ;
