pmc:AshtarTransmissionAshtarReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The work's claim that the messages of 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages are from Ashtar"@en, "Die Behauptung des Werkes, die Botschaften vom 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages stammen von Ashtar"@de ;
    skos:definition "The work prints under the dates 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages a message signed by Ashtar, who speaks for the purpose of the group and of the visits: to save mankind from itself by stopping the explosion of hydrogen, which he calls a living element; directs the group to send the messages to its government and through it to all governments; gives the group instructions of its own; and issues the forecasts and warnings of the second half of the book."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim, not its truth. The citation names Van Tassel as author because that is what a reader can obtain; the title page itself says the book was radioed by other-world intelligences through him."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "George W. Van Tassel, who says the messages came to him in the group's sessions at Giant Rock and that he is the contact for this reception" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Ashtar, who names himself the commandant of the quadra sector of patrol station Schare over all projections and waves, from the message of 22 August 1952 the Vela quadra sector" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "By the account on pp. 16-17, Van Tassel learned to tune in to vibrations by long study of his own thought, then gathered a small group at regular scheduled meetings to add power to the reception; the message is spoken aloud through his physical body, which he likens to a loudspeaker, and taken down in shorthand, and he says it is given in words humans can understand. The publisher's note of the New Age printing, signed Franklin Thomas, adds that he receives in attunement with the frequency of the communicating intelligence, mostly while his body senses involuntarily, in a condition in which he does not know his hearers are there, sometimes with partial awareness of them. No record of the sessions other than the printed text is mentioned. Dated 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages. Ashtar arrives in the message of 18 July 1952 directly after Portla's announcement, unheaded by a new date. The message of 22 August 1952 is said to be for the group and not for the government. On 23 November 1952 Ashtar hands the contact back to the Seven Lights council, which sits on Shanchea; on 11 January 1953 he says the attunement is difficult. Several messages thank the group for keeping the contact against ridicule." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 30-48, messages of 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

