pmc:AshtarTransmissionAshtarNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ashtar"@en, "Ashtar"@de ;
    skos:definition "A being who signs a message of 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages in this work as the commandant of the quadra sector of patrol station Schare over all projections and waves, from the message of 22 August 1952 the Vela quadra sector."@en ;
    skos:note "The name the tradition carries. In this work Ashtar is first announced by Portla as the chief on his first entry into the solar system, speaks twenty times, signs most messages with love, and names above him a center, Schonling as Lord God over the third-dimensional sector, and the Seven Lights council, to which he hands the contact back. Powers he claims for station Schare and its ships, not offered as attainable by practice and therefore not entered as capacities: ships of light substance that cannot be trapped or shot down, visible only through the elements of the atmosphere and able to seem where they are not; 100,000 units a second put into operation at need; several thousand light beings set down in remote places to record events; several hundred light intelligences placed in physical bodies by a change of vibration; substations within the earth's vortex releasing half a million ventlas each; telepathic conversation at will with mortals in the higher light; a vortex of light energy to steady the planet."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ashtar" ;
    pm:nameRole "commandant of the quadra sector, later the Vela quadra sector, of patrol station Schare" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 30-48, messages of 18 July 1952 to 20 March 1953, twenty messages; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

