    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 30, message of 18 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionCouncilOfTheTwelveLordsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Council of the Twelve Lords"@en, "Council of the Twelve Lords"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named once by Portla beside Schonling, Saochane and the Seven Lights council."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Council of the Twelve Lords" ;
    pm:nameRole "a council named among the sources of inspiration, not further described in this work" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 30, message of 18 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionCouncilOfTheSevenLightsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Council of the Seven Lights"@en, "Council of the Seven Lights"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lata says the fleet is working to pass messages from Blaau by way of this council; the author calls it the group's regular contact center; Ashtar says on 18 July 1952 that the council brought the group together and on 23 November 1952 returns the contact to it on Shanchea; the author names the earth's satellite Shanchea and defers its explanation to his book of the same title."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Council of the Seven Lights" ;
    pm:nameRole "the group's regular contact center, a council located on Shanchea, the satellite of the earth" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 25, 30 and 44-45, messages of 16 May, 18 July and 23 November 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionLemAndCorNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lem and Cor"@en, "Lem and Cor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named once by Noot: the group can feel the beam more whenever it gathers, except while projections from Lem and Cor are coming in. Whether these are beings, places or stations the work does not say; entered as named sources because they send projections as the beings of Schare do."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Lem and Cor" ;
    pm:nameRole "sources of projections the group receives, not further described in this work" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 37, message of 17 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# The practices
#

pmp:AshtarTransmissionSelfStudy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling deliberately with one's own thought"@en, "Das bewusste Verweilen beim eigenen Denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The receiver's first step: spending much time on purpose with his thoughts, studying what makes him work, until he knows the unseen part of himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 15-16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning in to a vibration and holding the reception under control"@en, "Das Einstimmen auf eine Schwingung und das Beherrschen des Empfangs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dialing a wavelength as one tunes a receiver until a transmission comes through intelligibly, then keeping the effect under one's control; the method by which every message of the book is said to have been received."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16-17; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionGroupMeeting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding scheduled meetings of a small group for reception"@en, "Das Abhalten geplanter Sitzungen einer kleinen Gruppe zum Empfang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gathering a few interested people, as the receiver says he was told to do by an unseen intelligence, and meeting at fixed times to join effort in unity; later messages thank the group for keeping the contact and tell it to consolidate the center."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16, 32, 37-38 and 48; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionGradualAccustoming a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Getting used by degrees to a powerful vibration"@en, "Das allmähliche Gewöhnen an eine starke Schwingung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming accustomed step by step, with the co-operation of its source, to one persistent and very powerful vibration before taking down its messages."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionNaturalLiving a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the freedom of nature in the desert"@en, "Das Leben in der Freiheit der Natur in der Wüste"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living for years at Giant Rock in clean air and quiet nights, away from the cities, which the introduction credits with the author's finding of himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 10-11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionBreakingAutomaticLiving a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking the bonds of automatic living"@en, "Das Zerbrechen der Fesseln des automatischen Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting free of the mechanical routine of city life and civilisation, which the introduction makes open to anyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionInnerVoice a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Listening to the inner voice while reading"@en, "Das Hören auf die innere Stimme beim Lesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attending, while reading the book, to an inner voice that the introduction says will let the reader know truth when it appears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionReceivingTheRay a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sitting in session under a ray sent by the beings"@en, "Das Sitzen in der Sitzung unter einem von den Wesen gesandten Strahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being present at a meeting while a speaker says his fleet is raying the group a substance; Dulac and Portla each say this was done."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 29-30, messages of 6 and 18 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionJoiningHands a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Joining hands when gathered"@en, "Das Händefassen bei der Zusammenkunft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The one bodily act the messages prescribe: when the group gathers, its members join hands to receive the vibration of the substance beam."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 37, message of 17 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionPeaceThought a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting the beings with a thought of peace"@en, "Das Begegnen der Wesen mit einem Gedanken des Friedens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Approaching any of the light beings set down on earth while projecting the thought that one is friendly, as Ashtar advises on 12 September 1952; the conclusion widens it to greeting the beings with thoughts of love instead of jets, guns and fear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 40 and 51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionSkyWatching a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Watching the sky, above all at night"@en, "Das Beobachten des Himmels, besonders bei Nacht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spending time watching the sky, which several speakers prescribe for set months and which the author asks of his readers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 19, 24, 35 and 48; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionAppliedEffort a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Applied and undisturbed effort toward an all-dimensional sense"@en, "Die angewandte und ungestörte Bemühung um einen allseitigen Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sustained, undisturbed effort by which, the conclusion says, a man can grow beyond the three-dimensional illusion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 49-50; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionThoughtAsLine a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using thought as the line to the Ever Presence"@en, "Das Denken als Linie zur Immerwährenden Gegenwart gebrauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking thought not as intelligence but as a means of reaching the ever-present vibration, a thin line of light between true receptivity and inner being, as the closing reception teaches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 50-51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionPreparing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Consolidating the center and storing food against coming changes"@en, "Das Festigen des Zentrums und das Bevorraten gegen kommende Umbrüche"@de ;
    skos:definition "What Ashtar tells the group, in a message said to be for it alone: consolidate the center, work together without regard to private property, build what structures it can, and above all lay in food."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 37-38, message of 22 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenExplosion a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploding the hydrogen element"@en, "Das Sprengen des Elements Wasserstoff"@de ;
    skos:definition "The project the visits are said to have come to stop: the attempt of physicists to explode hydrogen, which Ashtar calls a living element of the air, the water and the body."@en ;
    skos:note "A practice of others that the work warns against or asks for, entered so that its caution, chain or condition of failure has an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 30-32 and 36-37, messages of 18 July and 15 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionAtomicDestruction a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using atomic power for destruction"@en, "Das Nutzen der Atomkraft zur Zerstörung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bomb tests and the building of ever larger means of destruction, set by the introduction, Kerrull and the conclusion against a universal law of action and reaction."@en ;
    skos:note "A practice of others that the work warns against or asks for, entered so that its caution, chain or condition of failure has an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 9-11, 22 and 49; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionSpaceFlightBeyondTheVortex a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flying out beyond the earth's vortex"@en, "Der Raumflug über den Wirbel der Erde hinaus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any human attempt at space flight past the moon, which Ashtar restricts on 23 November 1952."@en ;
    skos:note "A practice of others that the work warns against or asks for, entered so that its caution, chain or condition of failure has an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 44, message of 23 November 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionTrappingTheShips a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to trap or shoot down the ships"@en, "Der Versuch, die Schiffe zu fangen oder abzuschießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The authorities' attempts, which the messages report, to capture or bring down a ship to learn what it is made of."@en ;
    skos:note "A practice of others that the work warns against or asks for, entered so that its caution, chain or condition of failure has an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 23-24 and 33-34, messages of 2 May and 1 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:AshtarTransmissionAbandoningHydrogenWeapons a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving up the development of hydrogen weapons"@en, "Das Aufgeben der Entwicklung von Wasserstoffwaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The decision Blaroc asks of the governments before the other object of the visits will be disclosed."@en ;
    skos:note "A practice of others that the work warns against or asks for, entered so that its caution, chain or condition of failure has an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 35, message of 10 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# The capacities
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSeventhSense a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The seventh sense, the sense of being"@en, "Der siebte Sinn, der Sinn des Seins"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the receiver says he found by dwelling with his thought: the life substance of his true identity, which he calls a seventh sense, of being, and the unseen intelligence within that each can find who makes the effort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 15; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionUniversalReceptivity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receptivity to vibrations from all of space"@en, "Empfänglichkeit für Schwingungen aus dem ganzen Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "An inner instrument he says parallels radio and television without their breakdowns: receptive to every vibration in space without depending on any transmitting station."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 15-16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionUnboundedFlight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Flight beyond the atmosphere and freedom from fear of leaving the body"@en, "Flug jenseits der Atmosphäre und Freiheit von der Furcht, den Körper zu verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "He says he is not confined to the atmosphere to fly, that the universe is his to explore, that he is not afraid to leave his dense body, and that he has found unlimited true life while still inside it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionDiscerningVibrations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling true vibrations from discords"@en, "Wahre Schwingungen von Missklängen unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Separating the true vibrations from the discordant ones, which he says he found soon after he had the effect under control."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionGroupReceptivity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A receptivity strong enough for the beings to speak through"@en, "Eine Empfänglichkeit, stark genug, dass die Wesen durch sie sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more powerful, more sensitive and more easily controlled reception the meetings are said to build; Ashtar names building it as the group's purpose, so that the beings could speak to the planet through it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16 and 32; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionPainlessReception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving a powerful vibration without bodily discomfort"@en, "Eine starke Schwingung ohne körperliches Unbehagen empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Receiving the one persistent vibration in attunement and without physical discomfort, which he says he reached only after getting used to its power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16-17; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionTrueBeing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's true, eternal self"@en, "Das wahre, ewige Selbst finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finding one's true being and the reality of one's eternal self, which the introduction says the author found in the desert and anyone can find who breaks out of automatic living."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 10-11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionRecognizingTruth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing truth when it appears"@en, "Wahrheit erkennen, wenn sie erscheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing truth at sight by an inner voice, promised to the reader of the book."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionBodilyBenefit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A substance good for the physical body"@en, "Eine dem Körper zuträgliche Substanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "A substance Dulac says is rayed to the group and will be very much to the advantage of their mortal, physical bodies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 29; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionInnerPerception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Better reception and inner perception"@en, "Besserer Empfang und innere Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The better reception Portla says the rayed substance gives and the better inner perception Noot says his continuous beam gives."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 30 and 37; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionCrossingTheBorder a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching the vibratory level needed to cross the border"@en, "Die zum Überschreiten der Grenze nötige Schwingungsebene erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A level of vibration the group is said to be helped toward; the work does not say what border is meant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 26-27; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionContactThroughTheArc a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct contact through the arc"@en, "Direkte Verbindung durch den Bogen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contact passing from Blaau by way of the Seven Lights council to the group, worked toward in one message and congratulated as made in another."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 25 and 27; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionReceptionFromUni a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reception from Uni"@en, "Empfang von Uni"@de ;
    skos:definition "Receiving from Uni, which Tonla says radion projections of his fleet will help; the work defers Uni to a later book."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 27 and 45; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionContactAboard a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The receiver's contact taken aboard a ship"@en, "Der Kontakt des Empfängers an Bord eines Schiffes"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the title claims and the speakers assert twice: that the receiver's contact was aboard a ship far above the group and was returned. The opening essay says the receiver does not claim it himself; the beings claim it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 13 and 18-23; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionAllDimensionalSense a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "An all-dimensional sense that records the future"@en, "Ein allseitiger Sinn, der die Zukunft verzeichnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sense of being in all dimensions by which a man can record events to come no less than present and past ones."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 50; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSkyRevelation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Things revealed within consciousness while watching the sky"@en, "Im Bewusstsein Offenbartes beim Himmelsbeobachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the author promises a reader who watches the night sky and sees no saucer: other things will come to light within his consciousness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 48; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionContactWithTheEverPresence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with the Ever Presence"@en, "Verbindung mit der Immerwährenden Gegenwart"@de ;
    skos:definition "The contact with an infallible ever-present vibration, true to all and favouring no rank, which the closing reception says thought exists to reach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 50-51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSafeApproach a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Approaching the light beings without meeting their defence"@en, "Sich den Lichtwesen nähern, ohne ihre Abwehr auszulösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coming near one of the beings from Schare now on earth without setting off their defensive conditions; they say they will otherwise only retreat."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 40; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionTelepathicConverse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathic conversation with the beings of Schare"@en, "Telepathisches Gespräch mit den Wesen von Schare"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conversation through mental telepathy which Ashtar says the beings assigned to Schare can hold at will with mortals of earth who are in the higher light."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 34; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionHigherLight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being in the higher light"@en, "Im höheren Licht stehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The condition of those mortals with whom, Ashtar says, the beings of Schare can speak telepathically at will; the work does not say how it is reached."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 34, message of 1 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionOtherObject a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning the other object of the visits"@en, "Den anderen Zweck der Besuche erfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being told the second purpose of the beings' interest in the earth, which Ashtar and Blaroc hold back."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 33 and 35, messages of 1 and 10 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionImmediateChanges a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rapid changes in finance, the military and politics"@en, "Rasche Umbrüche in Finanzen, Militär und Politik"@de ;
    skos:definition "The changes Ashtar says are already under way in the conjunction of finance, the military and politics, against which the group is to prepare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 37-38, message of 22 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionCigarShips a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The cigar-shaped ships from a neighbouring planet"@en, "Die zigarrenförmigen Schiffe von einem Nachbarplaneten"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of three kinds of craft Molca says are watching the earth, some of them with intent that is not peaceful, and watched in turn by Schare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 23, message of 27 April 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionPublishedElsewhere a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Material from the meetings published under other titles"@en, "Material aus den Sitzungen unter anderen Titeln veröffentlicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Information others received at the group's meetings and printed under titles of their own, for which the author refuses responsibility."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# The yieldings
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSelfStudyYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling with one's thought is said to yield the sense of being, receptivity to all of space, and flight beyond the atmosphere"@en, "Das Verweilen beim eigenen Denken soll den Sinn des Seins, Empfänglichkeit für den ganzen Raum und Flug jenseits der Atmosphäre ergeben"@de ;
    skos:note "Reported as the receiver's own experience in the first person, offered as open to each who makes the effort."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionSelfStudy ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionSeventhSense, pmc:AshtarTransmissionUniversalReceptivity, pmc:AshtarTransmissionUnboundedFlight ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 15-16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionAttunementDiscerningYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Holding the reception under control is said to teach the telling of true vibrations from discords"@en, "Der beherrschte Empfang soll lehren, wahre Schwingungen von Missklängen zu unterscheiden"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionDiscerningVibrations ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionGroupMeetingYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Scheduled meetings in unity are said to add power and make reception more sensitive and controllable"@en, "Geplante Sitzungen in Einheit sollen Kraft hinzufügen und den Empfang empfindlicher und lenkbarer machen"@de ;
    skos:note "The instruction to gather the group is itself said to have come through one of the receptions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionGroupMeeting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionGroupReceptivity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16 and 32; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionGradualAccustomingYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Getting used by degrees to the vibration is said to allow its reception without discomfort"@en, "Das allmähliche Gewöhnen an die Schwingung soll ihren Empfang ohne Unbehagen erlauben"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionGradualAccustoming ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionPainlessReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 16-17; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionNaturalLivingYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Years of natural freedom in the desert are said to have let the author find his true being"@en, "Jahre natürlicher Freiheit in der Wüste sollen den Autor sein wahres Sein finden lassen haben"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionNaturalLiving ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionTrueBeing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 10-11; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionBreakingAutomaticLivingYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Whoever breaks out of automatic living is said to be able to find his eternal self"@en, "Wer aus dem automatischen Leben ausbricht, soll sein ewiges Selbst finden können"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionBreakingAutomaticLiving ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionTrueBeing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
