pmc:AshtarTransmissionAttunementAboardYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "In attunement the receiver's contact is said to be taken aboard and returned"@en, "In der Einstimmung soll der Kontakt des Empfängers an Bord genommen und zurückgegeben werden"@de ;
    skos:note "The claim of Lutbunn and Molca, the source of the book's title; the receiver disowns it as his own claim in the opening essay."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionContactAboard ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 13, 18 and 23; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionAppliedEffortYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Applied, undisturbed effort is said to develop an all-dimensional sense that records the future"@en, "Angewandte, ungestörte Bemühung soll einen allseitigen Sinn entwickeln, der die Zukunft verzeichnet"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionAppliedEffort ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionAllDimensionalSense ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 49-50; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSkyWatchingYielding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Watching the night sky is said to reveal things within consciousness even when no saucer is seen"@en, "Das Beobachten des Nachthimmels soll auch ohne gesichtete Untertasse Dinge im Bewusstsein offenbaren"@de ;
    skos:note "The promise is built so that the obvious failure, seeing nothing, counts as success of another kind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AshtarTransmissionSkyWatching ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AshtarTransmissionSkyRevelation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
