#
# The chains
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionPeaceThoughtPresupposed a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Approach the light beings only with a thought of peace"@en, "Den Lichtwesen nur mit einem Gedanken des Friedens nahen"@de ;
    skos:note "Ashtar's advice of 12 September 1952, to be passed on to anyone who might by chance come upon one of the several thousand beings said to have been set down in remote places."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:AshtarTransmissionSafeApproach ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:AshtarTransmissionPeaceThought ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Any approach in another frame of mind meets at once with defensive conditions; the beings say they mean no harm and will act otherwise than by retreat only to protect themselves." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 40, message of 12 September 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionHigherLightPresupposed a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathic conversation with Schare only for mortals in the higher light"@en, "Telepathisches Gespräch mit Schare nur für Sterbliche im höheren Licht"@de ;
    skos:note "A restriction without a stated consequence: the beings can speak at will with mortals in the higher light, and the work says nothing of others."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:AshtarTransmissionTelepathicConverse ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:AshtarTransmissionHigherLight ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 34, message of 1 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionEffortPresupposed a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Each must make the effort to find the unseen intelligence within"@en, "Jeder muss die Bemühung leisten, um die unsichtbare Intelligenz in sich zu finden"@de ;
    skos:note "The opening essay says science can never see life or mind unmixed, that each can find it within, and that the effort has to be made by each himself before the effect comes; no consequence of omission is named beyond not finding it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:AshtarTransmissionSeventhSense ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:AshtarTransmissionSelfStudy ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 15; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionAbandoningHydrogenPresupposed a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The other object of the visits only after hydrogen weapons are given up"@en, "Der andere Zweck der Besuche erst nach dem Aufgeben der Wasserstoffwaffen"@de ;
    skos:note "Blaroc's condition of 10 August 1952; Ashtar had said on 1 August that the authorities do not ask what the other object is but only how to destroy the ships."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:AshtarTransmissionOtherObject ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:AshtarTransmissionAbandoningHydrogenWeapons ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 33-35, messages of 1 and 10 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# The cautions
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionReceptionErrorsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathic reception is bound to err, and events will show the errors"@en, "Telepathischer Empfang muss irren, und die Ereignisse werden die Irrtümer zeigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's note, before the messages: in a new field such as reception by telepathy errors cannot be avoided, coming events will expose errors in the receptions printed here, and they are printed as received all the same."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning against the work's own content, set before any forecast. It makes every failed forecast that follows readable as an error of reception rather than of the source, and it is the only place in the book that names reception itself as able to fail."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), author's note, before p. 9, in the later printing of the same edition that adds an annotation dated 1 September 1955; the New Age printing has a publisher's note in its place; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionColouringCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Received messages take the colour of the receiver's own speech"@en, "Empfangene Botschaften nehmen die Färbung der Sprache des Empfängers an"@de ;
    skos:definition "The publisher's note, signed Franklin Thomas: as with most such communications and with automatic writing, what the speaking intelligence impresses on the receiver often takes on the receiver's own habits of speech and language."@en ;
    skos:note "A warning from the publisher and not from the receiver or the speakers. It puts the wording of every message partly on Van Tassel, which is the question pmc:AshtarTransmissionAshtarReceiving leaves open."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), publisher's note, before p. 9, in the New Age printing only; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionBurningVibrationsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Many vibrations can burn up the body that receives them"@en, "Viele Schwingungen können den empfangenden Körper verbrennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The receiver says he grew cautious by experience because many of the vibrations he tuned in could burn out his physical body, which he calls his cabinet."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 16; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Exploding hydrogen will end life on the planet"@en, "Das Sprengen von Wasserstoff wird das Leben auf dem Planeten beenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ashtar on 18 July 1952: the bombs of plutonium and uranium split an inert element, but hydrogen is a life-giving element, and its explosion will put out life on earth and make the planet a cinder, as happened once before in this solar system when the planet Lucifer was torn apart. On 15 August he adds that the release of free hydrogen will send flames across many parts of the planet for a moment and that those in authority, and their own families, will not escape."@en ;
    skos:note "The governments are to be told and to tell all other nations; the beings say they will otherwise put an end to every project connected with it. On 14 November 1952, three days after newspapers announced a hydrogen bomb, Ashtar says the report given to the people is partly false and that an isotope does not count as an atomic element; the author adds that physicists then said the device was not the hydrogen bomb. Tested at pmc:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenTest."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenExplosion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 30-32, 36-37 and 44, messages of 18 July, 15 August and 14 November 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionAtomicReboundCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Destruction by atomic power rebounds on those who use it"@en, "Zerstörung durch Atomkraft schlägt auf ihre Urheber zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kerrull calls destructive atomic power a folly that will strike back at the users; the introduction asks whether man will meet the rebound tomorrow; the conclusion calls the reaction, by universal law, the cataclysmic balance for wrong action, visible in the ruins of earlier civilisations."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionAtomicDestruction ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 11, 22 and 49; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSpaceFlightCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Space flight beyond the earth's vortex ends any return"@en, "Raumflug über den Wirbel der Erde hinaus beendet jede Rückkehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ashtar on 23 November 1952: man's conquest of space is limited to the moon, and any attempt to go beyond the earth's vortex will end every chance of returning to earth."@en ;
    skos:note "The author adds that the message gives no reason and that the lack of knowledge about space may keep the reason beyond comprehension."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionSpaceFlightBeyondTheVortex ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 44-45, message of 23 November 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionThoughtAloneCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Thought alone fails when most needed, and old events scar its line"@en, "Denken allein versagt, wenn es am meisten gebraucht wird, und alte Ereignisse vernarben seine Linie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The closing reception: thought is not intelligence, is hemmed in by others' opinions and will let one down at the moment of greatest need; many past events can scar the line of light and lead off the path; only light is the eternal source."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionThoughtAsLine ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 50-51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionTreasonCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Received information could expose the receiver to a charge of treason"@en, "Empfangene Mitteilungen könnten den Empfänger dem Vorwurf des Verrats aussetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blaroc says much the center could pass on is held back because a security law of the receiver's nation could bring him under the penalty for treason, and that they will give nothing that puts him in danger."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:AshtarTransmissionAttunement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 35, message of 8 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionImmediateChangesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Prepare for rapid changes, above all by storing food"@en, "Sich auf rasche Umbrüche vorbereiten, vor allem durch Vorräte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ashtar to the group alone on 22 August 1952: consolidate the center, work together without regard to private property, build what structures are possible, and above all store food because of fast changes now striking the conjunction of finance, the military and politics."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:AshtarTransmissionImmediateChanges ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 37-38, message of 22 August 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionCigarShipsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Some cigar-shaped ships do not come in peace"@en, "Manche zigarrenförmigen Schiffe kommen nicht in Frieden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Molca: a part of the cigar-shaped craft from a neighbouring planet watch the earth without peaceful purpose, and Schare watches them as closely as it watches the earth."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:AshtarTransmissionCigarShips ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 23, message of 27 April 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionPublishedElsewhereCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The receiver answers for this reception and not for others' publications from the meetings"@en, "Der Empfänger steht für diesen Empfang ein und nicht für Veröffentlichungen anderer aus den Sitzungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The last paragraph but two of the conclusion: Van Tassel accepts all responsibility for having been the contact of this reception and none for others who have used information received at the meetings and are publishing it under other titles."@en ;
    skos:note "A warning about the corpus itself, within a year of the first message: the reception was already being carried out of the group by others."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:AshtarTransmissionPublishedElsewhere ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 51; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# The conditions of failure
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionClotaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: ships to be watched for from May to August 1952"@en, "Vorhersage: Schiffe von Mai bis August 1952 zu erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clota tells the group to watch the skies in the months May to August."@en ;
    skos:note "Dated. The author says more saucers were seen in those months than ever, including over Washington; entered as a sign at pmc:AshtarTransmissionWashingtonSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 19, message of 7 March 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionNomaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a buzz of the globe, an interception and a landing"@en, "Vorhersage: ein Überflug des Globus, ein Abfangen und eine Landung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Noma says the Pentagon will shortly have a great deal to puzzle over, that the beings will give the globe a buzz and hope not to be met head on, and that they will intercept and land when ready."@en ;
    skos:note "The buzz has no date, the landing none either. The author reads the buzz as the sightings over Washington of 26 to 28 July 1952, three months later; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionLetterSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 20, message of 6 April 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionLeektowPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a top world leader's death, bringing great strife"@en, "Vorhersage: der Tod eines der höchsten Führer, der großen Streit bringt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leektow says a leader at the very top will die and the earth will be shaken by great strife."@en ;
    skos:note "Undated. The author writes that to his knowledge this forecast has not come true; it is the one forecast the work itself reports as unfulfilled, and Luu's message in the same session says the transmission was broken off."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 21, message of 11 April 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionKerrullPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: prolonged illness from the following week's experiment"@en, "Vorhersage: lange Krankheit durch das Experiment der folgenden Woche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kerrull says that through inaccurate calculation many will be ill for a long time because of an experiment set for the following week."@en ;
    skos:note "Dated to the week after 19 April 1952. The author says the message came days before atomic tests near Las Vegas and that newspapers have reported a rapid rise in pernicious anemia; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionAnemiaSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 22, message of 19 April 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionClatuPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a landing, and official acknowledgement of higher authority"@en, "Vorhersage: eine Landung und die amtliche Anerkennung höherer Autorität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clatu tells the group to watch the east for the next four months, says the Pentagon will soon decide that the beings are of higher authority as well as higher intelligence, and says they will land."@en ;
    skos:note "The watch is dated to four months from 2 May 1952; the landing and the official decision have the term very near future."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 23-24, message of 2 May 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionHuldaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: more fireballs"@en, "Vorhersage: mehr Feuerkugeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hulda says the beings of Blaau are returning and more fireballs will be seen."@en ;
    skos:note "Undated; the author says fireballs were then seen over the northwestern states; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionFireballSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 24, message of 9 May 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionKletarcPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a famous woman, a September crisis and July aggression in the Far East"@en, "Vorhersage: eine berühmte Frau, eine Krise im September und Aggression im Fernen Osten im Juli"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kletarc, asked for tomorrow's news, says a woman known worldwide will be drawn into a controversy leading to international conflict, that the nation will reach a crisis in September, and that July will bring fresh aggression in the Far East."@en ;
    skos:note "Two parts dated to months of 1952. The author does not comment on this message."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 26, message of 23 May 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionKleacPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: much bloodshed in July 1952"@en, "Vorhersage: viel Blutvergießen im Juli 1952"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kleac says July will see much blood shed."@en ;
    skos:note "Dated; no comment by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 27, message of 11 June 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionToltaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a rogue in high office fatally struck within the week"@en, "Vorhersage: ein Schurke in hohem Amt binnen der Woche tödlich getroffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tolta says within a week a rogue holding high government office will be fatally struck."@en ;
    skos:note "Dated to the week after 14 June 1952; no comment by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
