pmc:AshtarTransmissionReaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a ship passing over the group within minutes"@en, "Vorhersage: ein Schiff überfliegt die Gruppe binnen Minuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rea says they are over Texas at an altitude of 70 thousand feet and will cross above the group within a few minutes; Qel the day before says the group will see more of them if it watches."@en ;
    skos:note "Timed to minutes; the author reports two luminous streaks seen; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionStreaksSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 28, messages of 28 and 29 June 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionKlactaPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: the most unpredictable weather ever seen"@en, "Vorhersage: das unberechenbarste Wetter, das je gesehen wurde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Klacta says the most unpredictable weather ever seen is coming in the immediate future."@en ;
    skos:note "The author points to later crop failures and weather extremes; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionWeatherSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), pp. 28-29, message of 3 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionBetthPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: a good earth shake"@en, "Vorhersage: ein ordentliches Erdbeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Betth tells the group to be ready for a good shake of the earth."@en ;
    skos:note "Undated; the author says it came seventeen days later at Tehachapi and on through Bakersfield; see pmc:AshtarTransmissionTehachapiSign."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 29, message of 4 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenProjectsPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: hydrogen projects will cease or be eliminated"@en, "Vorhersage: Wasserstoffprojekte werden eingestellt oder beseitigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ashtar says the explosion of life-giving atoms will stop, or the beings will eliminate all projects connected with it."@en ;
    skos:note "No date. The consequence of the explosion itself is entered as a caution and tested at pmc:AshtarTransmissionHydrogenTest; this node is the separate forecast that the projects will end."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a forecast with an outcome in the public world, so that its not coming to pass would fall on the reception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
