#
# The signs of success
#

pmc:AshtarTransmissionWarmFluidSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A warm fluid felt over the body under Dulac's ray"@en, "Ein warmes Fließen über den Körper unter Dulacs Strahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "After Dulac says his ray is on the group, the author reports that all of about 23 members present felt the same sensation, as if warm fluid were run over their bodies."@en ;
    skos:note "A bodily sign in the group, announced by the message moments before."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success and not as a condition of failure: it is reported after the event as confirmation, and nothing in the work says what would have counted against it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:AshtarTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AshtarTransmissionIRodeAFlyingSaucer ;
    dcterms:source "George W. Van Tassel, I Rode a Flying Saucer! The Mystery of the Flying Saucers Revealed, second edition, revised and enlarged (Los Angeles: New Age Publishing Co., 1952), p. 29, message of 6 July 1952; read in the full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:AshtarTransmissionSubstanceFeelingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the substance beam when joining hands"@en, "Das Fühlen des Substanzstrahls beim Händefassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Noot says the group may sense the substance more keenly whenever it gathers, by joining hands."@en ;
    skos:note "Announced in advance and left to the members to report."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success and not as a condition of failure: it is reported after the event as confirmation, and nothing in the work says what would have counted against it."@en ;
